---
title: Eight Can Taco Soup
servings: 6
time: 4 hours
tags: soup, chicken, mexican, slow-cooker, dinner
cuisine: Mexican-American
course: main
source: taco_soup.png (From Aimee Roth)
---

Drain and rinse @black beans{1%can}(15 oz), @pinto beans{1%can}(15 oz), and @sweet corn{1%can}(15.25 oz).

Drain @canned white chicken breast{1%can}(12.5 oz).

In a #slow cooker{}, add the drained beans, corn, chicken, @cream of chicken soup{1%can}(10.5 oz), @petite diced tomatoes{1%can}(14.5 oz), @medium enchilada sauce{1%can}(10 oz), @chicken broth{1%can}(14 oz), and @taco seasoning{1%package}.

Stir all ingredients together until well combined.

Cover and cook on low heat for ~{4%hours}.

Serve hot with optional @shredded cheese{}, @sour cream{}, and @tortilla strips{}.
